{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts","id":1314408,"title":"10,000 Year Daiklaives and the Equivalent N/A Artifacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-25T17:18:54-07:00","id":1314408,"title":"10,000 Year Daiklaives and the Equivalent N/A Artifacts","content":"So page 159 has &quot;10,000 year daiklaives&quot; under the description of N/A Artifacts. I've tried searching for various threads and not seen a lot on how to design these. <br /> <br /> According to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/940727-n-a-artifacts-how-to\">this</a>, people mention not just giving N/A artifacts more powerful stats (I'm unclear if that's still a thing or not) but to give the item a narrative power that warps the story.<br /> <br /> I'm not clear at all on artifact design, as deconstructing the &quot;rules&quot; by which all of the items is too time consuming for me at the moment. 2E for it's warts, had a clear guideline in Oadenol's Codex on what a 3 dot vs 5 dot artifact stats could be. Btw, I found a good list of 1E and 2E canon exalted artifacts <a href=\"http://segmarian.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Exalted/Artifacts/Canon_List\" target=\"_blank\">here.</a> <br /> <br /> In 3rd, so far we've only seen Warstriders as N/A artifacts, and they have limitations in the form of hearthstones and maintenance. <br /> <br /> I've seen some examples on the boards, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1167563-ereshkigal-artifact-n-a-soulsteel-daiklave\">Erishkigal </a>comes to mind, as well as others in the artifact design thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> The reason I bring this up is that I have a Supernal Craft Twilight and a Supernal Melee Dawn in my Solar game. The twilight can now make N/A artifacts in 2 rolls 99.6% of the time. They have access to a vault of 1st age materials, and want to make some N/A artifacts. (He bought the charm that lets him get up to 20xp after making 5 N/A artifacts.) <br /> <br /> The Dawn is a bodyguard with all of the guardian style charms for protecting other people. He asked about a Daiklaive that could break other daiklaives when using the &quot;defend other&quot; action. <br /> <br /> Twilight wants to make a bow of some kind, while the Eclipse PC wants a fancier Thrown weapon. <br /> <br /> As for Armor, the PC's are curious about it, but no concrete ideas. They like the idea of powerful things, but don't want &quot;I win&quot; buttons.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this are welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T17:28:54-07:00","id":1314411,"title":"","content":"Artifact N/A: These artifacts are plot devices governed<br /> by Storyteller fiat, capable of accomplishing legendary<br /> miracles unlike anything else in Creation. Their<br /> Evocations do not simply have more power and mechanical<br /> advantage than those of lesser artifacts, but instead<br /> allow their wielders to accomplish things no other artifact<br /> could. They cannot resurrect the dead or enable<br /> time travel, but beyond that, they accomplish anything,<br /> flouting major conventions of the setting. Unlimited<br /> number of Evocations.<br /> <br /> Arms of the Chosen. Basically, this means that instead of trying to think &quot;more power&quot;, you should probably think &quot;weirder&quot; and &quot;rules-breaking&quot;. If we took the Mantle of Brigid as a potential N/A Artifact example, maybe its first Evocation allows you to immediately learn a sorcerer's shaping ritual by defeating them in battle, sorcerous competition, or studying under them; as the tree goes on, it allows you to cast spells you haven't learned under certain conditions, to absorb successfully &quot;blocked&quot; or countered/distorted spells to gain Sorcerous Motes equal to that spell's cost, to spend SM in order to gain initiative bonuses, or to add dangerous clauses to spells in order to make them even more powerful, with its Capstone being &quot;Access the Solar Circle of Sorcery&quot; if non-Solar, and for Solars and Infernals something more akin to &quot;Instantly cast a Solar Ambition 2 or lesser working without need to pay XP, once a story, even if the story passes it cannot be reset until you make an actual Working of the same Circle and Ambition as the one you used this Evocation for&quot; or w/e. <br /> <br /> Point being, they're powerful but they're more about &quot;scale&quot; and breaking setting conventions in their niche areas. Not to say they can't get some really potent mechanics, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T18:20:29-07:00","id":1314419,"title":"","content":"so I'll pimp my thread and some of my work out a bit since you mentioned my Ereshkigal.<br /> <br /> first, you can check my homebrew thread here; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/119997-flare-s-homebrew-thread\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...omebrew-thread</a><br /> <br /> and I have a Storyteller's Vault product featuring a powerful Artifact 5 weapon here; <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/256547/Gyhominad-and-Glorybringer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...d-Glorybringer</a> <br /> <br /> But with that out of the way, to discuss your real question, I'll highlight what I think makes something 'level up' as an artifact. I'll just talk about the difference between Artifact 3 and Artifact 5 and N/A, as Artifact 4 can fit into the middle there easily.<br /> <br /> To me, an Artifact 3 can offer a new way to fight, but won't push the boundaries of it, or it can just be a decent series of powers that doesn't highlight you as a fighter. Meanwhile, an Artifact 5 or N/A, on the opposite side of the scale; it should both offer you new ways to engage in combat, and be powerful in doing so. Then, to me, what would push an artifact over 5 to N/A is either the presence of a large or at least decent amount of charms that can be learned with no Experience cost, or a similar effect that applies for free. In Ereshkigal, you can see it in the seals, which grant increasing power as a baseline effect. For a different Artifact 5 I'm working on, it involves a series of charms learned no by spending Experience, but by leaning into the legend of the spear; a massive, powerful Direlance called Earth Breaker-, as an army-scattering natural disaster that sends men and beasts to the ground and creates earthquakes and landslides.<br /> <br /> For instance, your Dawn Bodyguard, just as he's the one who really seems to have an idea, if you're making an Artifact N/A Sword for him, I'd actually suggest looking into a few reference sources. I've been on a Devil May Cry kick lately, so to me, I'd look right to two ideas there; the Yamoto and Royal Guard style.<br /> <br /> Just as some hypothetical abilities such a sword might have;<br /> <br /> The Exalt can summon Phantoms that defend other allies without needing to be next to them, allowing him to defend more then one person at once. I'd put this with something like an Initiative Cost where the Exalt makes Phantoms with their paid Initiative in 'phantom' Initiative, and if the shade has that much Initiative damage done to it, it is destroyed.<br /> <br /> From there, I would make charms that give you benefits for having so many phantoms out; representing your Phantoms combining with you into powerful attacks with a Decisive Damage booster, or giving you the ability to exchange places with your phantom as a surprise effect to defend your allies. Then we have to look at his other effect; destroying weapons. If I was going to make a part of the weapon something learned by expanding and living in the legend, I'd make that; with charms that benefit from the Exalt disarming opponents rather then decisively attacking them leading to them learning new charms for disarming or defeating a foe without incapacitating them directly. This gives the Exalt a reward for following the play patterns that they themselves want to encourage, and lets them expand their abilities without having to pick charms that may not always be relevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically, with Artifact 5s an N/As, I'd look at this; they should be useful for the character's combat style in that they offer the ability to shore up weaknesses and enhance strengths, then they should also offer either a new way to engage with the system that is generally outside the bounds of how that style of Exalt interacts with the system (A Solar Swordsman able to be in multiple places at once), and be very good in doing such a thing, or offer the ability to gain free 'power' by enticing the Exalt to work alongside the legend of that weapon and rewarding them with more Evocations for it..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T21:29:59-07:00","id":1314882,"title":"","content":"Vance\u2019s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1080642#post1080642\">spitball example</a> two years ago of an N/A weapon was one that slays an army in a single strike and raises it as a zombie army under your control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T22:27:31-07:00","id":1314889,"title":"","content":"There's not really a way to make N/A weaponry that doesn't make the wielder broken in at least some ways. Some sample Evocations could include :<br /> <br /> <u>Guardian Daiklave :</u><br /> -Reflect a source of uncountable damage directed at your ward back at the attacker or another valid target.<br /> -Shatter all the currently attuned artifacts of an attacker, making them unusable until artifact level repairs are performed.<br /> <br /> <u>Crafter Bow : </u><br /> -Fire an arrow which turns into any projectile you are able to craft yourself mid-flight, including projectiles which would be considered First Age Wonders i.e. implosion bolts.<br /> -Fire an arrow which instantly builds a small outpost, warship or any similar large-scale structure equivalent to a superior project where it lands.<br /> <br /> <u>Fancy Eclipse Thrown Weapon :</u><br /> -Throw a Chakram between 2 enemy forces, severing any positive ties between them and creating defining Ties of enmity between them for the Scene.<br /> -Fling a throwing knife that will find and strike their intended target anywhere within extreme range so long as the target holds a Major Tie towards you, including by crossing boundaries between worlds when possible (such as going through a shadowland or entering a spirit's sanctum)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 05-28-2019, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T08:44:59-07:00","id":1315186,"title":"","content":"Great suggestions everyone. I don't have a lot of time for custom creating evocations, but this has given me a good place to start. More ideas are welcome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T08:54:52-07:00","id":1315193,"title":"","content":"I'd talk to the players. They may know what effect they want to have and if you have that all you have to do is filter it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T03:47:50-07:00","id":1315654,"title":"","content":"Not sure how helpful this will be but here goes.<br /> <br /> When I introduce N/A artifacts I'd rather my PCs be intimidated and unsure how to use it than unimpressed. I favour uncontrollable power that the wielder learns to use efficiently (or safely!) through Evocations rather than efficiency building towards raw power. <br /> <br /> Though my N/As tend to be things my players found rather than made, hence its easier for me to give them a monkey's paw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T20:29:56-07:00","id":1315795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts?p=1315654#post1315654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how helpful this will be but here goes.<br /> <br /> When I introduce N/A artifacts I'd rather my PCs be intimidated and unsure how to use it than unimpressed. I favour uncontrollable power that the wielder learns to use efficiently (or safely!) through Evocations rather than efficiency building towards raw power.<br /> <br /> Though my N/As tend to be things my players found rather than made, hence its easier for me to give them a monkey's paw.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you willing to share what your N/A's have been and how they were used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T09:38:55-07:00","id":1315884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts?p=1315795#post1315795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are you willing to share what your N/A's have been and how they were used?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I've only ever tried my hand at making one N/A Artifact, and that was a Starmetal eye prosthesis Artifact based on the Rinnegan from Naruto. It basically screwed a lot with the cycle of reincarnation, and the body and surroundings of the bearer, though it's still not complete and thus I haven't showed it to anyone or tested it yet. N/As are pretty much a justification for going batshit crazy on Evocations and giving a character a lot of power, though sometimes at a scale or magnitude a tad too much to control at first. I wouldn't make all or even most of them monkey's paws, but some (like Karvara) work better that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T07:12:41-07:00","id":1317177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts?p=1315795#post1315795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you willing to share what your N/A's have been and how they were used?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main one is a cursed Daiklave called Atansis Kohl.<br /> <br /> The sword has a will of its own to the point she\u2019s more a support NPC than equipment, she can lend any and all of her Evocations to her bearer if she wants to. The problem is that by human standards she\u2019s a narcissistic psychopath that wants people to fight, kill and die in order to try and possess her in the hands of a Dawn Caste who considers any death unacceptable.<br /> <br /> So, he\u2019s limited by what he can ask of her because he\u2019s trying to curb her more negative traits by appealing to her ego rather than indulging her bloodlust. He mostly uses her as a talisman to make enemy combatants forget why they\u2019re actually there and instead focus their efforts upon trying to claim the sword for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T07:58:47-07:00","id":1317183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts?p=1315795#post1315795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are you willing to share what your N/A's have been and how they were used?</div> </div> </div> </div>One that I have drafted up is an unassuming necklace of glass beads, each glowing with a different light or flashing between several. The story behind it was the necklace housed the memories of ancient Eclipse and his pilgrimage to commune with various Incarna, Yozi, and various other powerful spirits on a quest to understand Divinity(Basically any patron of the Exalted). What the necklace basically did in terms of Evocations was give you access to a number of powerful Solar Spells each one based off a Spirit, in a grand display on what you call true divine magic. Like to list a few spells, Luna's was similar in function to Incomparable Body Arsenal, where you could use and switch between Luna's Archetypes for various benefits and build Evocations off those, The Elemental Dragons one was a buffed up version of Summon Elemental, which allowed you to create and command a Lesser Elemental Dragon as well washing the landscape with elemental Essence thus changing the surroundings to an environmental hazard, while the Yozi Malfeas one would allow you to temporarily summon a whole neighborhood of the Demon City, along with any 1st and rarely 2nd Circle Demons that was dwelling there, who if you manage to get under your contract were under you command. Big powerful spells like that.<br /> <br /> Of course to even use those spells is a quest in itself. To even attune to the necklace you had a Solar Circle Sorcerer, with every spell having a Special Activation Rule that you must accomplish before gaining access to the Spell, thus making sure that it take a long time before you were able to get all the spells, if ever. If you not a 3CS you can still get access to you patrons spell but only theirs, and you need to still accomplish the special activation rule.<br /> <br /> In any case thats what I have detailed anyway. Hope it helps","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T21:19:28-07:00","id":1317966,"title":"","content":"One of the Ideas I like about N/A artifacts is since they are not limited so much by rules they can be a way of making a mortal being comparable to an Exalt. We know Bagrash Kol was a mortal man and with the Eye he had an empire that eclipsed the Early Realm without an army of Dragonblooded. I like to think the eye gave him access to Invocations that allowed him to dip into solar scale charms. While others failed using the eye. So I like to think for Instance you could have a Keyblade be an Artifact N/A that essentially makes the Wielder an Exalt but tied to the Artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T23:28:19-07:00","id":1317986,"title":"","content":"In my last game there were N/A Hearthstones, formed from the Elemental Poles. The Eye and Seven Despairs was seeking them, to use their amazing power to connect to Creation and... Probably be overwhelmed by it, having very very very negative effects on the environment. But mostly because he was trying to imbue the Underworld with the Power of Life and Creation and end with its existence.<br /> <br /> He was planning to put them on his Gauntlet, which conveniently had 5 hearthstone slots","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13031,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","user":"Clophiroth","date":". 06-12-2019, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T01:33:33-07:00","id":1317994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts?p=1317986#post1317986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my last game there were N/A Hearthstones, formed from the Elemental Poles. The Eye and Seven Despairs was seeking them, to use their amazing power to connect to Creation and... Probably be overwhelmed by it, having very very very negative effects on the environment. But mostly because he was trying to imbue the Underworld with the Power of Life and Creation and end with its existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> He was planning to put them on his Gauntlet, which conveniently had 5 hearthstone slots</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh you cheeky bugger! This reminds me of an idea I had a couple years ago. Basically a primo level Solar Sorcerer Crafter made 10 eggs, out of the 5 Jades, And one of Soulsteel, one of Starmetal, one of Moonsilver, one of Orichalchum and one of Adamant. He also Sorcerously birthed a Pantheon of Gods as his avatars/Familiars, and left Creation with a caravan of thousand Score Mortal Souls to create his own Universe.<br /> <br /> I figured each egg would be like a level 5 Artifact that expanded mastery over their materials Purview. He was deciding what to do because the Deliberative was balking at his schemes, so he went to have a chat with Ligier, one duel later he was out of his slump missing an Eye and finally at peace. He took his Pantheon and had one thousand Score followers to commit ritual suicide and took their spirits with him to create somewhere he could explore and create in peace(aka in complete Tyranny). Each Egg was Worldshaking and his Pantheon helped in their Creation and when used in Unison with his solar might he could do impossible things. And when not in use each member of his Soul Pantheon guards an Egg and it represents their Authority over and aspect of Creation, like the God of Death holding the Soulsteel egg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T13:00:59-07:00","id":1384000,"title":"","content":"After a Hiatus my Exalted game might come back, so I thought I'd bump this for other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 04-30-2020, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T17:02:07-07:00","id":1384058,"title":"","content":"I tend to look at Wuxia/Xianxia Novels for inspiration such as Emperor's Domination, King of Gods, Invincible/Invincible Conqueror, Dragon Marked War God, Martial World/True Martial World, etc...<br /> <br /> Curoch, Iures, and the Ka'Kari from the Night Angel Trilogy by Brent Weeks<br /> Holdrun Cube, Kanai's Cube, Sword of Justice, Scroll of Fate, Black Soulstone, Spear of Valor, etc... from Blizzard's Diablo<br /> Chain Veil, Immortal Sun, Blackblade, etc... from Magic the Gathering<br /> The Dragon Amulet of the Spirit Monks from Bioshock's Jade Empire<br /> Vault Hunter abilities, most notably the Sirens for different Evocations, from Gearbox Software's Borderlands<br /> The Three Heavenly Treasures from Martial World/True Martial World (Magic Cube, Grandmist Bead, and Purple Card)<br /> Ring of Lucis, Royal Arms, and Armiger from Final Fantasy XV<br /> The Masks from Legend of Zelda: Majora's Mask (Deku, Goron, Zora, Giant, etc...)<br /> Create a Daiklaive based on the Forgotten Realms Moonblade that can only be wielded by a Specific Exalt and his subsequent reincarnations with each Incarnation that wielded it bestowing a Power<br /> Pieces of Eden from Ubisoft's Assassin's Creed<br /> Three Headed Monster, Three Winged Staff, and Three Lobed Burning Eye that form the Scepter of Power from the Black Trillium (Julian May, Andre Norton, Marion Zimmer Bradley)<br /> Ribbon Device, Eye of the Gods, and Sarcophagus from Stargate<br /> Primal Stones and the Sunforge from Netflix's The Dragon Prince<br /> <br /> <br /> ::The Radiant Pagoda of the Uncrowned King::<br /> Floor of the Eastern Wood<br /> Floor of the Western Water<br /> Floor of the Northern Air<br /> Floor of the Southern Fire<br /> Floor of the Central Earth<br /> Floor of the Many-Faced Moon (Lunars/Luna)<br /> Floor of the Star-Cloaked Vault (Sidereals/Maidens)<br /> Floor of the One True King (Solars/UCS)<br /> Floor of the Kings in Hell (Yozi/Infernals)<br /> Floor of the Kings in Shadow (Abyssals)<br /> Floor of the Forge-born King (Autochtonia)<br /> Floor of the Kings from Beyond (Wyld)<br /> <br /> Each &quot;Floor&quot; is a separate Artifact that will automatically merge with additional Floors found. Each Floor can be banished Elsewhere and re-summoned to your location like a Cache Egg. The Floors will only merge when you have attuned to multiple Floors and have them Elsewhere. Once they merge they cannot unmerge unless they are unattuned while Elsewhere, in which case they will leave Elsewhere and randomly appear anywhere within the bounds of the Exalted Universe (Malfeas, Yu-Shan, Wyld, Underworld, Autochthonia, Far Shore, etc...).<br /> <br /> Altogether, the Pagoda is a portable NA Manse independent of Leylines and Demesnes. Each Floor grants it's own Hearthstone and share of Powers. Without obtaining multiple floors, one might assume the wondrous treasure is nothing more than a portable manse of the relevant Aspect for the Floor they possess. If the Pagoda is fully assembled, who knows what power it might possess in addition to the benefits of a Manse untied to Geomancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T00:00:38-07:00","id":1384114,"title":"","content":"Some examples from previous editions of N/A artifacts were like, the Five Metal Shrike, a nearly indestructible hypersonic intelligent star fighter with a primary weapon cable of destroying a city in one shot. The only personal scale artifact N/A I can think of is this thing:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://campagna-exalted.obsidianportal.com/wikis/aidenweiss\" target=\"_blank\">https://campagna-exalted.obsidianpor...kis/aidenweiss</a><br /> <br /> Those aren\u2019t even all of its powers. It also forms a unique N/A hearthstone for its bearer, custom tailored to that character, which they get to keep for all time. Having a campaign where your PCs are cranking out like 10 of those things so everyone gets 2-3 would be complete insanity. That\u2019s when I\u2019d start instituting hard rules about the exotic components required for it. You might have all the magical materials that you could want, but for X thing you\u2019re making you\u2019re going to need one of Mela\u2019s actual scales, freely given. I don\u2019t want to punish my players or stop them from feeling epic, but going from zero to everyone walking around with the Aidenweiss as a weapon, a similarly legendary set of armor for protection, flying the Five Metal Shrike with the Eye of Autochthon and the Mantle of Brigid rattling around in the cargo hold is just way too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T00:34:33-07:00","id":1384118,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">In my game Paths of the Maker, the whole second 'season' was devoted to the creation of an N/A artifact called the Maker's Flame. I'll use my player's words here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Montserrat\">At rest, the Maker\u2019s Flame is a thin, vertically symmetical, palm-sized pentagonal prism of unnaturally clear and smooth diamond-like crystal. The eminent craftsmen of the First Age called this synthetic godmetal, \u2018Adamant\u2019 - the purest of its kind. </span></span> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Montserrat\">Within it is suspended a perfect white flame that dazzles and bewitches those that look upon it with its unearthly beauty. The ethereal matter in which it floats is a resurrected solution of a dead element that was slain and perverted by the Celestial Exalted at the end of the Time of Glories, much like those primordial demiurges that fell to them. It is an element of glorification, and it only remains inactive within its container because the surrounding flame and crystal alike can be refined no further.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Montserrat\">When the crystal is placed before a character\u2019s brow and attuned for ten motes, it dissolves into a burning sigil - The Word of Making, once spoken at the birth of the world. From the Word, a crown of white fire encircles the wearer. Its flames are difficult to gaze upon directly, not because they are bright, but because within them are contained the potentials for impossible things - every spark and tongue is a thought of splendor, and they promise that a future of miracles made real belongs to the one who wears them.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <br /> The Maker's Flame can initiate those who wear it into sorcery, provided they've constructed many artifacts. On top of that, its evocations supercharge the wearer's Crafting abilities, basically turning them into a demiurge who can perform crafting projects without the need for raw materials, or wrench a whole city out of the ground. They can transform matter into other types of matter.<br /> <br /> One notable weakness of the Maker's Flame is that it cannot conjure raw magical materials. No conjuring Jade or Orichalcum or anything like that.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T04:19:33-07:00","id":1384163,"title":"","content":"Hi, I wrote an N/A Flame Piece using a piece of prose I wrote a few years ago as inspiration, mostly in response to this thread. Since I haven't written for Ex3 in at least a year; don't play it that much, the mechanics will probably need to be polished, but here goes:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zLwn4jhBRB87Cm-pM4c18EYq8f0XikljBkj-uKoYv88/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Amita-Ha, the Weapon of Dead Justice</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T12:28:59-07:00","id":1384240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts?p=1315654#post1315654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how helpful this will be but here goes.<br /> <br /> When I introduce N/A artifacts I'd rather my PCs be intimidated and unsure how to use it than unimpressed. I favour uncontrollable power that the wielder learns to use efficiently (or safely!) through Evocations rather than efficiency building towards raw power.<br /> <br /> Though my N/As tend to be things my players found rather than made, hence its easier for me to give them a monkey's paw.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Saber's Excalibur from <i>Fate/Stay Night</i> would be rated N/A. Since, if I remember correctly, using that thing at all always meant a torrential outpouring of destruction, and using it for anything else required mastery.<br /> <br /> An N/A rating would actually makes much more sense for its lore than a 5-dot, really. Since it was supposed to be a divine weapon made by the spirit of the world itself from humanity's collective dream of &quot;Sword&quot;, and possibly humanity's wishes for victory. Since the weapon's title is &quot;Sword of Promised Victory&quot;, and all humans would instantly recognize the sword's identity upon seeing it, even if they had never heard of Excalibur before.<br /> <br /> And while it can't raise those it kills as zombies, it can in fact slay an entire army in one attack. As well as the castle they might be hiding inside. And any dragon that might also be inside the castle.<br /> <br /> Its not the sort of weapon that any player should be able to start with, like a 5-dot sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T02:50:34-07:00","id":1384816,"title":"","content":"Yeah, to me the Eye of Autochthon in the 1st edition Storytellers Companion is still the quintessential N/A for the game, There's a lot of N/As I disliked because they were essentially occupying that space because 6 dot artifacts didn't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:06:37-07:00","id":1384851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts?p=1384816#post1384816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, to me the Eye of Autochthon in the 1st edition Storytellers Companion is still the quintessential N/A for the game, There's a lot of N/As I disliked because they were essentially occupying that space because 6 dot artifacts didn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could that have been something of an abstraction? Without the lost techniques and infrastructure of the First Age you were as capable of making such 6 dots as you were of making the Eye? (that is, not at all) (at least without epics quests far beyond what would be required if you just continued the success ramping up and increased the required components by one)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T19:31:07-07:00","id":1384986,"title":"","content":"Recently looking over some 2E Exalted sources I thought of something similar to Odin's High Seat, creating an Artifact NA Throne that widened the range of Awareness Charms to anywhere in a Single Direction if not all Creation. The idea was precipitated by thinking about Scion's Ultimate Perception when looking through the MoEP: Abyssal Charms (Piercing Gaze of the Unmaker), it's Mirror (Eyes of the UCS), and the Abyssal Larceny Charm Reality Subverting Gesture. The Ultimate Ink Monkey's Collection had the Daystar Arsenal bit, and Sky Conquering Mea gave me the idea of expanding the scope of particular Charms to hundreds of miles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T21:29:50-07:00","id":1385001,"title":"","content":"N/A Artifacts can do many a thing. I wrote the below as inspiration, not limitation. <br /> <br /> An N/A Artifact would not break the attacker's blade parrying in protection of the player's ward, it would break his will to fight. An N/A Artifact would not strike true from afar when thrown but would disappear from the player's hand, reappearing in inconspicuous places, tripped over and forgotten, preventing the fate the player's aggression seeks to halt. An N/A Artifact would be capable of protecting the player's vitals as well as his reputation. An N/A Artifact could reason with a player, granting wisdom in war and peace, seeming to all who viewed their ruler as one who measured her words before proclaiming the law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:11:57-07:00","id":1385004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts?p=1385001#post1385001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">N/A Artifacts can do many a thing. I wrote the below as inspiration, not limitation.<br /> <br /> An N/A Artifact would not break the attacker's blade parrying in protection of the player's ward, it would break his will to fight. An N/A Artifact would not strike true from afar when thrown but would disappear from the player's hand, reappearing in inconspicuous places, tripped over and forgotten, preventing the fate the player's aggression seeks to halt. An N/A Artifact would be capable of protecting the player's vitals as well as his reputation. An N/A Artifact could reason with a player, granting wisdom in war and peace, seeming to all who viewed their ruler as one who measured her words before proclaiming the law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm thing is I could see some Less then N/A artifacts doing some of these, especially depending on the interpretation of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:23:42-07:00","id":1385006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314408-10-000-year-daiklaives-and-the-equivalent-n-a-artifacts?p=1384851#post1384851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could that have been something of an abstraction? Without the lost techniques and infrastructure of the First Age you were as capable of making such 6 dots as you were of making the Eye? (that is, not at all) (at least without epics quests far beyond what would be required if you just continued the success ramping up and increased the required components by one)</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that was the intention, I just don't care for it at all. The game allows you to start play with an artifact up to 5 dots because you could be rocking the panopoly of a First Age Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T15:37:04-07:00","id":1385469,"title":"","content":"I recently remembered the reason why I originally never considered Saber\u2019s Excalibur to be a N/A artifact.<br /> <br /> Gilgamesh\u2019s Ea, which objectively outclasses it. Whereas Excalibur is classified as an anti-fortress weapon, Ea is classified as an anti-WORLD weapon, allegedly capable of destroying entire planes of existence if given enough time to charge. Certainly capable of destroying the temporary worlds created by Reality Marbles (if he doesn\u2019t hesitate to draw the thing, because of pride).<br /> <br /> <br /> But I suppose that both can be NA artifacts if Ea\u2019s least output has certain drawbacks compared to Excalibur\u2019s best output.<br /> <br /> For one thing, Saber\u2019s master was struggling to provide her with enough energy, whereas Gilgamesh was consuming an entire orphanage\u2019s worth of children\u2019s souls for fuel on top of having a better master, so Ea might have been far more expensive and Gilgamesh simply had more energy to spare.<br /> <br /> For another, Ea\u2019s least output might still inflict far more incidental damage to the surroundings than Excalibur. Certainly, the weapon\u2019s attack wave seemed far less precise.<br /> <br /> <br /> But perhaps most importantly, Ea can only ramp UPWARDS, and when you already start with more than enough power to destroy fortresses, anything more quickly becomes diminishing returns. Especially if destroying the world (or even just one whole Direction) requires such a long and alarmingly obvious charge-time that Heaven itself can and will intervene to stop you. Which turns Ea\u2019s later Evocations into plot devices more than character tools.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Excalibur could theoretically scale DOWNWARDS, so that it becomes more versatile to use in a wider variety of situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}